<h2>How a 1965–73 Mustang VIN is laid out</h2>
<p>Classic Mustangs use an 11-character VIN, for example <strong>5F07K135945</strong>.</p>
<div class="not-prose overflow-x-auto my-6"><table class="w-full text-sm text-left text-silver-300 border border-white/10"><thead class="bg-white/5 text-silver-200"><tr><th class="p-3">Position</th><th class="p-3">Example</th><th class="p-3">Meaning</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr class="border-t border-white/10"><td class="p-3">1</td><td class="p-3">5</td><td class="p-3">Model year, last digit (5 = 1965)</td></tr><tr class="border-t border-white/10"><td class="p-3">2</td><td class="p-3">F</td><td class="p-3">Assembly plant</td></tr><tr class="border-t border-white/10"><td class="p-3">3–4</td><td class="p-3">07</td><td class="p-3">Body serial code</td></tr><tr class="border-t border-white/10"><td class="p-3">5</td><td class="p-3">K</td><td class="p-3">Engine</td></tr><tr class="border-t border-white/10"><td class="p-3">6–11</td><td class="p-3">135945</td><td class="p-3">Consecutive unit number (each plant starts at 100001)</td></tr></tbody></table></div>
