white/10"><td class="p-3">M</td><td class="p-3">1970–71</td><td class="p-3">351 Cleveland 4-barrel</td></tr><tr class="border-t border-white/10"><td class="p-3">Q</td><td class="p-3">1969–70</td><td class="p-3">428 Cobra Jet</td></tr><tr class="border-t border-white/10"><td class="p-3">Q</td><td class="p-3">1971</td><td class="p-3">351 Cobra Jet</td></tr><tr class="border-t border-white/10"><td class="p-3">R</td><td class="p-3">1969–70</td><td class="p-3">428 Cobra Jet Ram Air</td></tr><tr class="border-t border-white/10"><td class="p-3">R</td><td class="p-3">1971</td><td class="p-3">Boss 351</td></tr><tr class="border-t border-white/10"><td class="p-3">S</td><td class="p-3">1967–69</td><td class="p-3">390 V8 4-barrel</td></tr><tr class="border-t border-white/10"><td class="p-3">T</td><td class="p-3">1965–70</td><td class="p-3">200 inline-6</td></tr><tr class="border-t border-white/10"><td class="p-3">U</td><td class="p-3">1964½</td><td class="p-3">170 inline-6</td></tr><tr class="border-t border-white/10"><td class="p-3">Z</td><td class="p-3">1969–70</td><td class="p-3">Boss 429</td></tr></tbody></table></div>
<p>Where our sources disagree on a letter, we leave it out of the decoder instead of picking one.</p>
<h2>The 1964½ question</h2>
<p>Early Mustangs built from spring 1964 were titled as 1965 models, so their VIN starts with 5. Engine codes D, F and U, used only on those early cars, are a strong hint that you’re looking at a “1964½.”</p>
<h2>Verify more than the VIN</h2>
<p>Trim, paint, axle and transmission codes are on the door data plate, not in the VIN. For high-value cars (K-code, Boss, Cobra Jet, Shelby), confirm the hidden partial VINs and documentation, and consider a Marti Report.</p>
<h2>Frequently asked questions</h2><h3>What does a K in a Mustang VIN mean?</h3><p>On 1965–67 Mustangs the fifth character K means the 289 High Performance V8 rated at 271 hp.</p><h3>How do I know if my Mustang is a 1964½?</h3><p>Early cars are titled as 1965 models. Engine codes D, F or U, used only on 1964½ production, are a strong hint; production date and other details confirm it.</p><h3>Does the Mustang VIN show the color and trim?</h3><p>No. Paint, trim, axle and transmission codes are on the door data plate, not in the 11-character VIN.</p>
